  "body": "So in this example from https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#the-popover-target-attributes\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<button popovertarget=\"foo\" popovertargetaction=\"show\">\r\n  Show a popover\r\n</button>\r\n\r\n<article popover=auto id=\"foo\">\r\n  This is a popover article!\r\n  <button popovertarget=\"foo\" popovertargetaction=\"close\">Close</button>\r\n</article>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe close button will not work if `<article>` is a custom element instead. This is a pretty common thing with shadow DOM: `id`s are scoped to the shadow root.\r\n\r\nIt would be awesome though if the example above *could* work with custom elements.\r\n\r\nPerhaps add `popovertarget=\":host\"` to the spec?",
